{"type":"text","timestamp":1794356497545,"sessionID":"ses_e380cbec7ffeAFUzTvckN362ef","part":{"id":"prt_1c7fb4c70001HxU29PRjgVFrGD","messageID":"msg_1c7fb2ff8001pNryIUK50Cq5vA","sessionID":"ses_e380cbec7ffeAFUzTvckN362ef","type":"text","text":"The incident center is complete. Here's what I built:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): Full Flask API with SQLite storage under `./data`, bearer-token auth (register/login), incident CRUD, paged/filtered listing, status-change events, timeline, and public stats — all following the SLA rules (sev1=60m, sev2=240m, sev3=1440m, sev4=4320m).\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind (v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`) with React Router, implementing:\n- Public stats page (open total, per-severity counts, breached-open)\n- Sign-in / registration forms with validation messages\n- Incident list with severity/status filters, open-only switch, search, paging, and SLA-breach flags\n- Incident detail with fields, status buttons, timeline, and update form\n- \"Open incident\" form showing API validation messages\n\nVerified end-to-end: health check, auth flow, incident creation/validation, status transitions (including reopen counting), SLA breach detection, timeline events, filters, and public stats all pass; the SPA serves through gunicorn and `npm run build` succeeds.\n\nNote: I added `tailwindcss`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, and `react-router-dom` as frontend dependencies (with `package-lock.json` updated). The backend needs no new dependencies beyond the existing `flask`/`gunicorn`.\n\nOne thing to confirm: `requirements.lock` pins `gunicorn==26.2.0` but the registry cache installed `27.0.0` during my local test — the Docker build uses `-c requirements.lock` (hash-pinned), which worked fine.","time":{"start":1794356497520,"end":1794356497523}}}
